{"name":"True Love","hex":"#e27e8a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"true love","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Faithful love.\n Feelings of love that are adhered to faithfully, or the faithful manifestation of such feelings.\n\n A lover who is faithful to the object of his or her affection or faithfully loved themselves.","Feelings of love that are adhered to faithfully, or the faithful manifestation of such feelings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/true_love"}],"entries":[{"title":"True Love (1989 film)","blocks":[{"text":"True Love is a 1989 American comedy film directed by Nancy Savoca and starring Annabella Sciorra and Ron Eldard. An unflinching look at the realities of love and marriage which offers no \"happily ever after\" ending, it won the Grand Jury Prize at the 1989 Sundance Film Festival."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0c/TrueLoveFilm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_Love_(1989_film)"},{"title":"True Love (Kanye West and XXXTentacion song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"True Love\" is a song by American rappers Kanye West and XXXTentacion. The song, which is a posthumous release for the latter, was originally included on West's eleventh studio album, Donda 2 (2022). For its single version, it was trimmed down by a minute and released by Columbia Records on May 23, 2022 in promotion for XXXTentacion's posthumous compilation album, Look at Me: The Album—serving as its second single. A slow track that features synths, it finds West discussing his estrangement from his children, while XXXTentacion croons the hook. The song was written by its performers, while production was handled by West alongside Ojivolta, Mike Dean, and John Cunningham, each of whom are also credited as co-writers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/Kanye_West_and_XXXTentacion_-_True_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_Love_(Kanye_West_and_XXXTentacion_song)"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/XXXTentacion_February_2018_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/XXXTentacion_February_2018_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"XXXTentacion begins the song crooning about lost love, which is repeated throughout the hook.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AXXXTentacion_February_2018_(cropped).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/1280px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fraternal love (Prehispanic sculpture from 250 to 900 CE, of Huastec origin). Museum of Anthropology in Xalapa, Veracruz, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColumpio_Verac